Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete only when all of the following are true:

Android NDK r27 is fully configured and builds successfully.
liboqs, OQS-OpenSSL, OpenSSL, and WebRTC are compiled and integrated as native libraries.
All approved QGuard Helix cryptographic algorithms are implemented and verified.
Secure messaging, encrypted voice/video calls, and Quantum Vault operations use the native cryptography layer.
Android Keystore protects device-bound secrets and key material.
JNI interfaces are minimal, secure, and well documented.
The project builds without warnings or errors in Android Studio.
Performance benchmarks demonstrate low-latency cryptographic operations suitable for production use.
Security reviews, memory safety checks, and automated tests all pass successfully.
Documentation is complete, accurate, and ready for long-term maintenance.

